From 218322b5b26978db90f0824771ae2b120bf60d36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Deng, Bing" <bing.deng@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:15:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix IMU buffer locking and duplicate init in laserMapping

Major bug fixes:
1. Move the mutex lock in imu_cbk and sync_packages so the shared
   buffer state is covered by the lock for its entire read/write
   window, not just the tail end of it.
2. Fix res_last never actually reaching its -1000 sentinel value
   because memset() truncates a float fill argument to a byte;
   replace it with std::fill and drop the leftover duplicate reset
   of point_selected_surf/res_last a few lines below the real one.
3. Check mkdir()'s return value when creating the log directory
   instead of silently ignoring failures, and wrap main() in a
   try/catch so a startup exception is logged instead of crashing
   the node outright.

Signed-off-by: Deng, Bing <bing.deng@intel.com>
---
 src/laserMapping.cpp | 94 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------------
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/laserMapping.cpp b/src/laserMapping.cpp
index 2a82a69..706ebe7 100644
--- a/src/laserMapping.cpp
+++ b/src/laserMapping.cpp
